<!--
The REST security domains.

These ArtifactGroups deliberately carry NO ArtifactAuthz: they are the path to
domain lookup that growerp.100.SecurityServices100.check#RestAccess reads. The
single guard that does carry an ArtifactAuthz is GROWERP_REST_GUARDED in
GrowerpSecurityData.xml, which calls that service for every REST leaf.

artifactName is a Java regex (nameIsPattern="Y") matched against the full
artifact name, e.g. /growerp/100/FinDoc. inheritAuthz is irrelevant on these
members and left at "N": they carry no ArtifactAuthz, so the framework never
authorizes anything through them. The value that matters is on the guard in
GrowerpSecurityData.xml, which is "Y" so an authorized endpoint carries through
to the service it invokes.

A domain may need SEVERAL members: artifactName is text-medium (255) and part of
the primary key, so one long alternation does not fit. check#RestAccess matches
against every pattern, so splitting one domain over several rows is equivalent.
Alternatives are longest first so that e.g. Courses is not shadowed by Course.

The 28 anonymous-* resources bypass authz entirely and need no domain.
-->
<entity-facade-xml type="seed">

    <moqui.security.ArtifactGroup artifactGroupId="GROWERP_BASE"
        description="Session, menu and messaging: reachable by every signed in user"/>
    <moqui.security.ArtifactGroupMember artifactGroupId="GROWERP_BASE"
        artifactTypeEnumId="AT_REST_PATH" nameIsPattern="Y" inheritAuthz="N"
        artifactName="/growerp/100/(MenuConfigurations|MenuConfiguration|Authenticate|Notification|ChatMessage|MenuItems|ChatRoom|MenuItem|AppUsed|Logout)(/.*)?"/>

